==============================================================================
1. What RDCL is
==============================================================================

RDCL (Ray Dust Craft Launcher) is a MODIFIED VERSION of HMCL
(Hello Minecraft! Launcher), distributed as an independent build that tracks
upstream HMCL releases. Upstream project: https://github.com/HMCL-dev/HMCL

Because RDCL is a work based on HMCL, the whole combined work is conveyed
under the terms of the GNU General Public License version 3 together with the
additional terms imposed by the upstream HMCL project (see section 3 below).
See LICENSE-GPL-3.0 for the full GPLv3 text.

==============================================================================
2. Dual licensing (per GNU GPLv3 section 13)
==============================================================================

GNU GPLv3 section 5(c) requires that the entire work based on the Program be
licensed as a whole under GPLv3 ("This License gives no permission to license
the work in any other way").

GNU GPLv3 section 13 additionally permits:

    "Notwithstanding any other provision of this License, you have
    permission to link or combine any covered work with a work licensed
    under version 3 of the GNU Affero General Public License into a single
    combined work, and to convey the resulting work."

RDCL therefore applies the following split:

  (a) Files derived from upstream HMCL — including everything under the
      HMCL/, HMCLCore/, HMCLBoot/, buildSrc/ and minecraft/ trees, and any
      other file originating from the upstream repository — remain licensed
      under GNU GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE Version 3 together with the upstream
      additional terms. Their original copyright headers are retained
      verbatim and MUST NOT be removed or re-labelled.

  (b) Files that are original to RDCL — patches/, scripts/, assets/rdcl/,
      .github/workflows/, this README/LICENSE material and other RDCL-only
      files — are offered under the GNU AFFERO GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE
      Version 3 (SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only). See
      LICENSE-AGPL-3.0 for the full text.

  (c) As a single combined work, the special requirements of the GNU Affero
      General Public License section 13 concerning interaction through a
      network apply to the combination as such. RDCL fulfils this by
      publishing the corresponding source of every binary release alongside
      the binaries in the same GitHub Release.

==============================================================================
3. Upstream additional terms (GNU GPLv3 section 7)
==============================================================================

The upstream HMCL project distributes its program under GPLv3 with the
following additional terms (quoted from docs/README_zh_Hans.md of HMCL):

  1. When you distribute a modified version of the software, you must change
     the software name or the version number in a reasonable way in order to
     distinguish it from the original version. (Under GPLv3, 7(c))

  2. You must not remove the copyright declaration displayed in the software.
     (Under GPLv3, 7(b))

RDCL complies with both:

  * Requirement 1 — the program is renamed "RDCL / Ray Dust Craft Launcher"
    and its version numbers carry a distinct "-rdcl" suffix, e.g.
    "3.17.0.362-rdcl".

  * Requirement 2 — no copyright notice has been removed. All original
    copyright headers of the upstream sources are preserved verbatim, and
    the upstream authors are credited in the application's About page.

